3. Revisionist is aggrieved with the said order dated 05.12.2022 and has assailed the same on various grounds which can be summarized as under:-
(i) That the Ld. Trial Court has gravely erred inbasing the impugned order on erroneous inference drawn without the perusal of the material on record and also without considering the totality of circumstances;
(ii) That the Ld. Trial Court has gravely erred in dismissing the discharge application filed by the revisionist without applying the test that whether the material on record prima facie is sufficient to frame charges or not while dismissing the discharge application;
(iii) That the Ld. Trial court has gravely erred in dismissing the discharge application filed by the revisionist casually and mechanically without stating any reason for doing so in as much as the discharge applcation dismissal order states nothing about legal reasoning for dismissed the said application;
(iv) That the Ld. Trial Court has failed to consider the broad probabilities of the case,
the total effect of the evidence and the documents produced before it;
(v) That the Ld. Trial Court has failed to appreciate the fact that the criminal proceeding is manifestly attended with malafide intention and proceeding is maliciously instituted with an ulterior motive for wreaking vengeance on the revisionist and to spite him due to private and personal grudges by dradding her innocent in laws in the proceedings;
Govindi Pant And Anr vs State Of Nct Of Delhi on 6 February, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/193735293/
2 Crl Rev No. 124/2023 Govindi Pant & Anr. Vs. State of NCT of Delhi & Anr. Page No.
3 of 9 (vi)

Hence,
Section 498A and Section 34 IPC do not constitute under these circumstances;
(viii) That the Ld. Trial Court has failed to appreciate the fact that the allegations in the FIR and other material accompanying the FIR do not disclose a cognizable offence qua the revisionists;
(ix) That the Ld. Trial Court ahs failed to appreciate the fact that the requirements under Sections 498A/406/34 IPC are not meted out to charge the revisionists.

